# oracle: pair spin/dipole/long 8.0 with kspace_style pppm/dipole/spin 1.0e-4 and kspace_modify gewald 0.25 mesh 8 8 8 (hybrid/overlay with spin/exchange 3.5), bcc iron 6x6x6 cells (432 random spins), nve/spin lattice frozen, the pressure tensor of the spin configuration at steps 0 and 5 (the pressure is the kspace virial: the spin pairs do not contribute with a frozen lattice)
# measured with native LAMMPS (black box), engine vs native fixture: thermo max relative error 2.7e-15 (absolute 4.4e-16) over pe, press and the six pressure components at steps 0 and 5. The case fixes kspace_modify gewald 0.25 mesh 8 8 8: with the automatic G-ewald and mesh (2 2 2, G 0.0705) the kspace virial and energy are ~1e-35 and ~1e-5 in both codes, which would not test the virial. Re-measured under Node 20: not needed (below 1e-8).
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=none rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           metal
atom_style      spin
dimension       3
boundary        p p p
atom_modify     map array
lattice         bcc 2.8665
region          box block 0.0 6.0 0.0 6.0 0.0 6.0
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 55.845
set             group all spin/random 11 2.2
pair_style      hybrid/overlay spin/exchange 3.5 spin/dipole/long 8.0
pair_coeff      * * spin/exchange exchange 3.4 0.02726 0.2171 1.841
pair_coeff      * * spin/dipole/long 8.0
neighbor        0.1 bin
neigh_modify    every 10 check yes delay 20
kspace_style    pppm/dipole/spin 1.0e-4
kspace_modify   gewald 0.25 mesh 8 8 8
fix             1 all precession/spin zeeman 0.001 0.0 0.0 1.0
fix_modify      1 energy yes
fix             2 all nve/spin lattice frozen
timestep        0.0001
thermo_style    custom step pe press pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             5
